Regarding the `executeAsyncTaskWithRetry` method, here's a skeleton implementation:

```java
public class DistributedFileStorageSystem {
    // ... constructor, fields, and other methods ...

    public <T> Future<T> executeAsyncTaskWithRetry(Callable<T> task, List<BackendService> backendServices, RetryStrategy retryStrategy, int maxRetries, long timeout) {
        ExecutorCompletionService<T> executor = new ExecutorCompletionService<>(Executors.newFixedThreadPool(backendServices.size()));

        for (BackendService service : backendServices) {
            Future<?> submitResult = executor.submit(task);
            Future<T> resultFuture = executor.take(); // blocks until a result is available or timeout expires
            resultFuture.whenComplete((result, exception) -> {
                if (exception != null) {
                    if (retryStrategy.shouldRetry(exception)) {
                        int retriesLeft = maxRetries - 1;
                        submitResult.cancel(true); // cancel the previous submission
                        if (retriesLeft > 0) {
                            executeAsyncTaskWithRetry(task, backendServices, retryStrategy, retriesLeft, timeout);
                        }
                    }
                }
            });
        }

        // ... handle completed tasks and return the result when all have been processed ...
    }
}
```

